joinCodeReply
	🔑 Join code for a new node, single-use, valid 10 minutes:

	fj-abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwx

	On the new machine, paste one line.

	*macOS, Linux (sh):*
	```fridolin node join fj-abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwx --core fridolin-core.example.ts.net:8766```

	*Windows (PowerShell):*
	```& "$env:ProgramFiles\fridolin\fridolin.exe" node join fj-abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwx --core fridolin-core.example.ts.net:8766```

	Core: fridolin-core.example.ts.net:8766. Add `--root PATH:rw` to share a folder, `--no-exec` to allow no commands (docs/NODES.md). Once it connects I'll tell you here, and `!approve <id>` lets it in.
joinCodeReply(box)
	🔑 Join code for a new node, single-use, valid 10 minutes:

	fj-abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwx

	On the new machine, paste one line.

	*A node in a box* (Docker; it asks for the rest):

	*macOS, Linux:*
	```curl -fsSL https://example.com/fridolin/0123abcd/container/box.sh | sh -s -- --registry ghcr.io/owner --version 0123abcd --core fridolin-core.example.ts.net:8766 --code fj-abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwx```

	*Windows (PowerShell):*
	```& ([scriptblock]::Create((irm https://example.com/fridolin/0123abcd/container/box.ps1))) -Registry ghcr.io/owner -Version 0123abcd -Core fridolin-core.example.ts.net:8766 -Code fj-abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwx```

	*Or natively*, with fridolin installed on it:

	*macOS, Linux (sh):*
	```fridolin node join fj-abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwx --core fridolin-core.example.ts.net:8766```

	*Windows (PowerShell):*
	```& "$env:ProgramFiles\fridolin\fridolin.exe" node join fj-abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwx --core fridolin-core.example.ts.net:8766```

	Core: fridolin-core.example.ts.net:8766. Add `--root PATH:rw` to share a folder, `--no-exec` to allow no commands (docs/NODES.md). Once it connects I'll tell you here, and `!approve <id>` lets it in.
